{
 "id": "AT-QA-02-04-skills",
 "tmp_base": "repo",
 "layer": "H",
 "owner": "skills",
 "note": "Q-ADAPTER QA-1, QA-2, QA-B2 (AT-QA-02, AT-QA-04, skills half): begin reads the queue mode through queue::lane, the one list parser; locate reads it from the setting alone and never runs the queue tool (no list call, no caps-cache write): queue_cmd empty -> \"queue\": {\"mode\": \"off\"} and `queue: off` with no exec and no queue_cmd trace; not executable -> degraded (not-executable), no exec; a tagged v1 reply -> on with the Queued: line and the lane in the stage meta; another schema -> degraded (schema), no Queued: line, no lane. lane adopt maps the adopt exit codes of tests/fixtures/queue/adopt-*: 0 -> `lane: <id>`, 3 -> `held holder=<sid> kind=<kind>`, 4 -> no-lane, 6 -> error, 2 -> unsupported, and passes --must-exist exactly when the cached list reply's commands hold adopt:must-exist.",
 "now": "2026-10-21T14:05:12+03:00",
 "tz": "Etc/GMT-3",
